 "sarvam_vocals": {
  "text": "Motion, motion, changing position of an object in time, velocity, acceleration, along a straight line. Come on to everything in the universe motion. We walk, we ride a bicycle, we run, we play. Air moves into and out of our lungs. Blood flows in arteries and veins, carry people, automobiles and planes. Water flowing down a dam. Leaves falling from trees. Earth rotates once every 24 hours. We fall round the sun once in a year. The sun, in motion in the Milky Way. Milky Way, moving within its local group of galaxies. Rectilinear motion, uniform acceleration, a set of simple equations, relative nature of motion, relative velocity, point objects, valid so far as size is much smaller than the distance it moves in a reasonable duration of time. Real life, good number of situations, sides neglected, without much error. Motion, motion, change in position of an object with time, velocity, acceleration along a straight line. ",
